	  PQCP_DEPLOYMENT_PASSPORT_PK_CHUNK / PQCP_DEPLOYMENT_PASSPORT_SIG_CHUNK
	  markers. The custody profile is fixed to demo and documented in
	  docs/passport-signing-custody.md: the key proves passport integrity
	  at the moment of signing, not device identity, and the secret key
	  signs exactly one message before being zeroized.

	  Unlike the other evidence options this option DOES execute
	  cryptographic operations (one ML-DSA-65 keygen, sign, and verify).
	  It does not alter public APIs, change ACVP wire formats, or alter
	  benchmark marker ordering.

